{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: forecasts systematically underprice realized levels by ~+2 to +5 EUR across most horizons; apply an upward level shift, larger in strong uptrends.",
    "Trend/acceleration under-capture: when the last 1–2 weeks show a rising regime, the model lags and misses upside momentum; add a positive trend adjustment proportional to recent slope (e.g., 5–10d MA slope).",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: underestimation tends to grow with horizon (weeks 2–4 especially); use a bias ramp (small uplift days 1–5, larger uplift days 10–30).",
    "Post-spike behavior: after sharp moves the model often mean-reverts too quickly and/or overshoots downward later in the path; dampen mean-reversion strength and cap downward corrections following upside breakouts.",
    "Volatility compression: forecast paths are smoother than outcomes and miss higher peaks; widen forecast distribution or add volatility scaling so highs/lows are less muted, especially around days 7–20."
  ]
}
